  "note": "Pinned, reproducible NCCI PTP release. Both ends of the build are pinned: `inputs` records each CMS release file's exact URL, byte size and SHA-256, and `output_sha256` records the bytes those inputs must produce. tools/build_ncci_ptp.py fetches EXACTLY these inputs (or the same files from a controlled immutable copy via NCCI_INPUT_DIR) and verifies every input checksum before parsing; tools/prepare_ncci.py then verifies the output checksum. A mismatch means the upstream release was rotated, replaced or corrupted -- do NOT rebuild silently: run `tools/build_ncci_ptp.py --refresh`, review data/sources/ncci_ptp.lock.proposed.json, and promote it in a reviewed commit. Pinning the inputs (not only the output) is what keeps a clean rebuild of this commit reproducible after CMS rotates a quarter, since CMS retains only the current and prior quarter. The builder is byte-deterministic for a given release (verified: a --refresh from these inputs reproduced output_sha256 exactly)."
